  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening IHP governance and transboundary water cooperation in Latin America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This element will support LAC Member States strengthening water security through IHP National Committees and enhanced cooperation. It will assist strengthening the governance of LAC&#x2019;s large transboundary surface and groundwater systems (e.g. Amazon, Plata, Guarani), whose sustainability is key to the SDGs. It will also promote cooperation, both within the scope of SDG indicator 6.5.2 and within regional and international processes. It will promote hydrodiplomacy and includes the organization of the regional meetings of IHP National Committees, World Water Day celebrations, WWAP&#x2019;s WWDRs regional launchings, and strategic actions with CILAC, CODIA, and Latin-American and world water fora, among others, to support LACs leading water policies and key initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
